sis the United States has seen in  generations and Matthew Desmond a  Princeton University professor who runs  the eviction lab project says if nothing  else changes and evictions continue as  normal and this public health crisis  will turn into a full-blown  crosses now the federal moratorium is  set to expire on July 25th housing  advocates are pushing for a national  moratorium for all renters not just  federally subsidized housing renters  they also want billions of dollars from  the government to help these renters out  by the way Rhonda Englander you know in  Idaho she did get her April rent covered  through a local charity she said she's  not sure what she's going to do about  her  875 dollar rent payment for May an  attorney for her complex told us that if  they forgave her rent they'd have to  forgive everybodies but he noted that  they have chosen not to evict anyone for  the month of April Tony forgiving  everybody's may be the only solution  we've got an economic crisis the last  thing we need right now is that to  become a homelessness crisis as well if  addictions skyrocket Anna thank you very  much
 

